Return false instead of asserting when no package id can be determined.

On aarch64 the package id comes only from sysfs. When sysfs CPU topology is
unreadable, as it is in some containers, no cpuinfo record gets a package id
and all of them reach __kmp_package_id_from_core_siblings_list.

That function asserts when the sibling mask is empty. __kmp_parse_cpu_list
returns an empty mask for an unreadable core_siblings_list, and for one
listing CPU ids at or above __kmp_xproc.

Returning false sends the caller through kmp_i18n_str_MissingPhysicalIDField
to __kmp_affinity_create_flat_map. Then the process gets a flat topology
rather than an abort.

Drop this patch once upstream fixes the assert. It is still present in
llvmorg-23.1.1.

--- a/openmp/runtime/src/kmp_affinity.cpp
+++ b/openmp/runtime/src/kmp_affinity.cpp
@@ -3208,7 +3208,10 @@ static bool __kmp_package_id_from_core_siblings_list(unsigned **threadInfo,
       return false;
     }
   }
-  KMP_ASSERT(threadInfo[idx][pkgIdIndex] != UINT_MAX);
+  if (threadInfo[idx][pkgIdIndex] == UINT_MAX) {
+    KMP_CPU_FREE(siblings);
+    return false;
+  }
   KMP_CPU_FREE(siblings);
   return true;
 }
